======================================================================
VS Code Remote-SSH terminal profile
======================================================================

For VS Code Remote-SSH, prefer configuring the integrated terminal profile
instead of forcing RemoteCommand for the whole connection. This lets VS Code
start its server normally, while new terminals still load remote-ssh.

Add this to the VS Code settings used for the remote host:

  {
    "terminal.integrated.profiles.linux": {
      "bash + remote-ssh": {
        "path": "bash",
        "icon": "terminal-bash",
        "args": [
          "--rcfile",
          "@INSTALL_DIR@/shell/rc.sh",
          "-i"
        ],
        "overrideName": true
      }
    },
    "terminal.integrated.defaultProfile.linux": "bash + remote-ssh"
  }
